[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Create only R0021–R0023 from the B0009 manifest assignments. Retain all
[stderr] +implementation gates; writing a runbook does not approve implementation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Context packet
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Read the assigned manifest and catalogue records, the SHARD-03 specification
[stderr] +sections, F014, and the runbook template.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Output list
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `../runbooks/R0021.md` through `../runbooks/R0023.md`, one per assigned IMP.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Validation procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Confirm metadata, provenance, ownership, dependencies, asset/audio assessment,
[stderr] +and canonical requirement links match the manifest before each write.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Checkpoint and update procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Record only B0009's completed output state after each validated R file. Retain
[stderr] +reserved IDs and repair only the failed output if validation fails.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Collision protection
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Stop if an assigned ID/path is owned by another contract or an accepted file
[stderr] +would be overwritten.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Stop condition
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Stop after R0021–R0023; do not create B0010 outputs or allocate further IDs.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.
