sment,\n+and canonical requirement links match the manifest before each write.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Record only B0009's completed output state after each validated R file. Retain\n+reserved IDs and repair only the failed output if validation fails.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Stop if an assigned ID/path is owned by another contract or an accepted file\n+would be overwritten.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0021\u2013R0023; do not create B0010 outputs or allocate further IDs.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.\n+- Each output retains gates and has complete provenance and asset/audio metadata.\n+- Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0010.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0010.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5392f950ea427e9569f2c1fce06b81bcdda801f0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0010.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0010\n+sequence: 14\n+title: Author accessibility, recovery, and evidence implementation contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only R0024\u2013R0026 from the B0010 manifest assignments while preserving\n+the SHARD-03 gates and the SHARD-04 handoff.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the assigned manifest/catalogue records, accessibility and recovery\n+specification sections, F014, and the runbook template.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0024.md` through `../runbooks/R0026.md`, one per assigned IMP.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Confirm metadata, provenance, dependencies, ownership, and explicit asset/audio\n+assessment against the manifest before each write.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Record only B0010's validated output state. Retain IDs on repair and do not\n+reallocate an incomplete contract.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Stop on any ID/path collision, accepted-work overwrite, or source mismatch.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0024\u2013R0026; do not expand SHARD-04 or create its B batches.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.\n+- Each output preserves gates, ownership, provenance, and asset/audio assessment.\n+- Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..74f4113c8df86558fd093230f0b14b6003956d66\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0004\n+sequence: 15\n+title: Continue bounded implementation-runbook authoring dispatch after SHARD-03\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one bounded dispatch iteration after D0003: expand at most one eligible\n+chapter into at most 250 IMP records, allocate ready contracts into at most ten\n+B batches of at most seven R outputs, then create one successor or final audit.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the project brief, canonical specification, catalogue, JSON/Markdown\n+ledger, D0003 checkpoint, and F014. Keep every human gate explicit; SHARD-05\n+remains held without recorded authorisation.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+Allocate only newly ready unassigned contracts and create exactly one successor\n+dispatcher while queued/authorable work remains, otherwise one final audit B task.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, chapter limit, unique monotonic IDs, dependency closure and\n+acyclicity, ownership, provenance, allocation uniqueness, and asset/audio metadata.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update both ledgers only after validation. Retain IDs on repair and never\n+overwrite, renumber, or regenerate accepted B/R work.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Verify every new ID/path is absent from the manifest and filesystem before use;\n+stop on collision, source conflict, or unresolved authority.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and one successor/audit;\n+do not recursively materialise later work.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs.\n+- Every created authoring task has objective, validation, checkpoint, stop, and acceptance criteria sections.\n+- Exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task is created after queue and ready-work review.\n+- IDs, ownership, provenance, dependencies, and asset/audio metadata are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\nindex 92a9491ce4d93779e85ecb200dc3ba4b420b8ff4..926e2b3fa009136848f375561ac3ff753514c400\n--- a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\n@@ -24,16 +24,22 @@\n     {\"id\":\"IMP-0017\",\"title\":\"Specify campaign progression and safe ending integration\",\"domain\":\"campaign\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0005\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"One town-to-dungeon-to-ending progression integration specifies safe checkpoints and a completable original campaign route.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0013\",\"IMP-0014\",\"IMP-0015\",\"IMP-0016\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/campaign/progression*\",\"tests/core/campaign/progression*\"],\"data\":